 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "This is Tessel (a Flask-like framework), and the mechanism is a \"template context injector\".\n\n**How `request`, `g` and `session` get in**\n- `_base_template_vars()` in `src/tessel/templating.py:21` is the default injector. It returns `g` and, when there is a request, `request`. Its comment says `session` stays the proxy, so it is available through the normal proxy.\n- `Scaffold.__init__` in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:182-184` pre-registers it: `template_ctx_injectors = defaultdict(list, {None: [_base_template_vars]})`.\n- `Tessel.fill_template_scope()` in `src/tessel/app.py:588` runs the injectors and updates the context dict in place. It runs the `None` (app-wide) injectors first, then those of the current request's bundles.\n- Values you pass to `render_template` override injected ones (`app.py:609-616`).\n- `_render()` and `_stream()` in `templating.py` (lines 123 and 164) call `fill_template_scope()` before every render.\n\n**Adding your own variables**\n- Use the `@ctx_injector` decorator, `Scaffold.ctx_injector` in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:549`. The function returns a dict, and its keys become template variables:\n  ```python\n  @app.ctx_injector\n  def inject_user():\n      return {\"current_user\": ...}\n  ```\n- On an app it applies to every template.\n- On a bundle it applies to templates rendered from that bundle's views.\n- `@bundle.app_ctx_injector` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:~648`) registers an injector from a bundle that applies to all templates.\n\nCaveat: the code at `scaffold.py:563` appends to the `None` key even on a bundle, which doesn't obviously match the \"bundle-only\" docstring. I didn't trace how bundles override this, so check that before relying on bundle-scoped injectors.",
